###  https://raphaffou.github.io/#readability-paper
<https://raphaffou.github.io/#readability-paper> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                          <https://schema.org/ScholarlyArticle> ;
                                                 <https://schema.org/about> <https://raphaffou.github.io/#llms> ,
                                                                            <https://raphaffou.github.io/#nlp> ;
                                                 <https://schema.org/isPartOf> <https://raphaffou.github.io/#jsi-internship> ;
                                                 <https://raphaffou.github.io/ns#approach> "Five open-weight LLMs, four corpora (three English, one Slovenian), no training at all: we vary only the prompt — its format, zero to three labelled examples per level, and whether the model answers directly or reasons first — and compare the best configuration with classical formulas and supervised models." ;
                                                 <https://raphaffou.github.io/ns#codeNote> "Code will be released after the review period." ;
                                                 <https://raphaffou.github.io/ns#label> "Readability with LLMs" ;
                                                 <https://raphaffou.github.io/ns#order> 1 ;
                                                 <https://raphaffou.github.io/ns#problem> "Readability formulas transfer poorly across genres and languages, and supervised models need annotated corpora that rarely exist for less-resourced languages such as Slovenian." ;
                                                 <https://raphaffou.github.io/ns#result> "Reasoning before answering brings large gains, especially for models that reason natively, and the first labelled example per level carries most of the few-shot benefit. The best configuration, with no training, beats every classical formula on the Slovenian textbook corpus and on WeeBit." ;
                                                 <https://raphaffou.github.io/ns#slug> "readability-llms" ;
                                                 <https://raphaffou.github.io/ns#stack> "Python; vLLM; open-weight LLMs; chain-of-thought; few-shot prompting" ;
                                                 <https://raphaffou.github.io/ns#status> "Preprint on arXiv · submitted to ECIR 2027, under review" ;
                                                 <https://raphaffou.github.io/ns#summary> "A systematic benchmark of open-source LLMs for readability assessment in English and Slovenian, the first to study how explicit reasoning and few-shot prompting change their predictions of discrete readability levels." ;
                                                 <https://raphaffou.github.io/ns#venue> "ECIR 2027" ;
                                                 <https://raphaffou.github.io/ns#venueUrl> "https://www.ecir2027.co.uk/"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                                 <https://schema.org/author> "Raphaël Thieffry; Matej Martinc" ;
                                                 <https://schema.org/datePublished> "2026-09"^^xsd:gYearMonth ;
                                                 <https://schema.org/name> "Assessing Readability with LLMs: The Role of Reasoning and Few-Shot Prompting" ;
                                                 <https://schema.org/url> "https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.24650"^^xsd:anyURI .


